chiaki-ng backport: keep the login PIN out of verbose logs.

Origin: https://github.com/streetpea/chiaki-ng commit
728d2b607abdda9fa85c4e36f56132e305dbf4cc ("Keep the login PIN out of verbose
logs", 2 November 2026), unchanged.
Licence of the patched file: LicenseRef-AGPL-3.0-only-OpenSSL (AGPL-3.0-only
with the OpenSSL exception), as in chiaki-ng.

The verbose hex dump of outgoing control messages included the login PIN
reply, which carries the console's login PIN in plain text. That one message
type is no longer dumped. Log output only; nothing sent changes.

Applies after 0001-0007 to the pin 0e16950165f06e5c3291537c2eeba6e852be7120.

diff --git a/lib/src/ctrl.c b/lib/src/ctrl.c
index 1e4dae0c..41b8e818 100644
--- a/lib/src/ctrl.c
+++ b/lib/src/ctrl.c
@@ -638,7 +638,8 @@ static ChiakiErrorCode ctrl_message_send(ChiakiCtrl *ctrl, uint16_t type, const
 
 	CHIAKI_LOGV(ctrl->session->log, "Ctrl sending message type %x, size %llx\n",
 			(unsigned int)type, (unsigned long long)payload_size);
-	if(payload)
+	// The login PIN reply carries the PIN in plain text, so keep it out of even verbose logs
+	if(payload && type != CTRL_MESSAGE_TYPE_LOGIN_PIN_REP)
 		chiaki_log_hexdump(ctrl->session->log, CHIAKI_LOG_VERBOSE, payload, payload_size);
 
 	uint8_t *enc = NULL;
